Register the geolocation system permission manager before the first profile.

Turning on os_level_geolocation_permission_supported made the browser die
during startup with SIGSEGV on CrBrowserMain, on a device where geolocation
had been working.

Building a profile builds its PermissionManager, and with the flag on
embedder_support hands geolocation to GeolocationPermissionContextSystem,
whose constructor does

  auto* m = device::GeolocationSystemPermissionManager::GetInstance();
  DCHECK(m);
  m->AddObserver(this);

with nothing but that DCHECK, which this build compiles out. The manager was
being registered from NotifyAuraShellBrowserStarted, which the adapter calls
from PostBrowserStart -- after profiles exist. So GetInstance() returned null
and AddObserver dereferenced it.

The constraint is tighter than "before anything asks for a position", which is
what the earlier comment claimed: it is before the first PermissionManager.
PreProfileInit is the hook that satisfies it, and it is where the equivalent
registration happens on the platforms that already had this flag.

The adapter's own entry point is split so that this happens on its own rather
than pulling the rest of PostBrowserStart forward with it.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51; chromium-154-harmonyos.patch does
not touch PreProfileInit, so the context is the pristine one.

Apply with:
  git -C /path/to/chromium/src apply /path/to/patches/ohos-geolocation-manager-init.patch

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
@@ -1506,6 +1506,10 @@
 
 void ChromeBrowserMainParts::PreProfileInit() {
   TRACE_EVENT0("startup", "ChromeBrowserMainParts::PreProfileInit");
+
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
+  chrome::ohos::EnsureAuraShellSystemPermissions();
+#endif
 
   media::AudioManager::SetGlobalAppName(
       l10n_util::GetStringUTF8(IDS_SHORT_PRODUCT_NAME));
